The nickname oobleck comes from a 1949 picture book by [[@dr-seuss|Dr. Seuss]], *Bartholomew and the Oobleck*. In the story, a bored king wants something new to fall from the sky, and his magicians produce a sticky green goo that gums up the whole kingdom.

Science teachers borrowed the name for cornflour and water, which is gloopy and a bit magical too. It's a favourite classroom experiment in India and the USA, partly because cornflour is cheap, safe and washes off. Families sometimes add a drop of food colouring to make it look more like the book.

{{story:dr-seuss}}

मणिपुर पहाड़ियों से घिरी एक हरी-भरी घाटी है, जो म्यांमार की सीमा के पास है। इसकी राजधानी इंफ़ाल है, और इसकी सबसे बड़ी झील [[@india-wonder-loktak|लोकटक]] अपने तैरते टापुओं के लिए मशहूर है। घाटी के लोगों, यानी मैतेई, में संगीत, युद्ध-कला और नृत्य की लंबी परंपरा है।

सबसे पुराने उत्सवों में से एक है लाई हराओबा, जिसका मतलब है 'देवताओं का आनंद-उत्सव'। *माइबी* नाम की पुजारिनें ऐसे नृत्यों की अगुआई करती हैं जो बताते हैं कि दुनिया और इंसानी जीवन कैसे रचे गए। माना जाता है कि मणिपुरी नृत्य की बहुत-सी कोमल चालें इन्हीं प्राचीन [[ritual|अनुष्ठानों]] से आई हैं।

{{story:northeast-india}}

Guru Nanak then set out on long journeys, called *udasis*, over more than 20 years. His companion was Bhai Mardana, a Muslim musician, who played the rabab, a stringed instrument, while Nanak sang.

The Janamsakhis, life stories written later, say they travelled across India and as far as Sri Lanka, Tibet, Mecca and Baghdad. Historians can't confirm every place, but they agree he travelled very widely and talked with Hindu and Muslim holy people. Like [[@mirabai-kabir|Kabir]] before him, he sang in the language of ordinary people.

{{story:golden-temple}}

Wilson Bentley was a farm boy in Jericho, Vermont, USA. In 1885, aged 19, he became the first person known to photograph a single snowflake. He attached a camera to a microscope and worked in freezing sheds, catching flakes on black velvet.

Over his life he photographed more than 5,000 snowflakes. No two of his pictures looked exactly the same. Neighbours called him "Snowflake Bentley". His pictures showed the world that six arms, again and again, were nature's rule.

